# UST.G3AF: Two-H First-Order Joint Graph/Coefficient Lift Theorem

## Status

`CLOSED_EXACT_FINITE_RING_FIRST_ORDER_TWO_COMPONENT_LIFT`

`UST.G3AE` proves that the selected second primitive-`H` graph can be
preserved by deforming the eta9 coefficient vector. This theorem adds the
independently selected first primitive-`H` graph and asks the stronger
question:

> Does one global eta9 coefficient lift contain both selected `H` graphs at
> once?

The answer is yes modulo `101^2`.

